  "variants": {
    "evolved": {
      "description": "A Brood Swarm grub: the same larva, fed. It carries the head the plain one gave up — a near-black rust dot at the front — over an amber body, and it is authored a third larger. The 1.3 is a texel budget and not a size: a consumer folds it into the texture and divides it back out when it asks for a world scale, so this variant is drawn at thirteen pixels in order to be sharp at whatever size it is asked for, and how big it actually lands is the game's call, not this document's. What the extra detail buys is that the head survives — at seven pixels a bigger, darker head was invisible next to the plain grub, which is why hue was carrying the whole distinction. This one does not spend itself on one hit: it latches, bites three times, and is thrown off backwards between bites still facing its mark, which is a thing only a drawing with a front can do.",
